<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Imperial raises half year shr, div.</title>
<headline>Imperial raises half year shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 25, 1996 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   96.6    vs 73.7</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     96.6    vs 73.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 38.0    vs 29.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   165.0   vs 96.8</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   228.6   vs 141.9</p>
<p>    Tax			 77.6    vs 48.1</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.4     vs 37.4</p>
<p>    Turnover		  3,816.1 vs 3,143.6</p>
<p>Div payable April 29</p>
<p>on register March 20</p>
<p>Full name: Imperial Holdings Ltd (industrial holding)</p>
<p>NOTE -  Although business conditions are likely to remain tight, the company said it was positioned to deliver good earnings growth.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
